  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Riemann Integration [S+N]\n\nGiven $f : [a, b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ and a partition $a = x_0 < x_1 < \\ldots < x_n = b$, the **upper sum** and **lower sum** are\n\n$$U(f, P) = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\left(\\sup_{x \\in [x_{i-1}, x_i]} f\\right)(x_i - x_{i-1}), \\qquad L(f, P) = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\left(\\inf_{x \\in [x_{i-1}, x_i]} f\\right)(x_i - x_{i-1}).$$\n\n$f$ is **Riemann integrable** on $[a, b]$ if $\\inf_P U = \\sup_P L$ as the partition mesh goes to zero. The common limit is $\\int_a^b f$.\n\nTheorem: every continuous function on $[a, b]$ is Riemann integrable. (The proof relies on Heine-Cantor uniform continuity from the previous notebook.)\n\nThis notebook visualises the upper/lower sums squeezing the integral, ties symbolic and numerical integration through Maxima, and shows the fundamental theorem of calculus.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 19,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Upper, lower, and midpoint sums\n\nTake $f(x) = x \\sin(x)$ on $[0, \\pi]$. With $n$ equal sub-intervals of width $h = \\pi/n$, compute the three classical Riemann sums.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "f_riem(x) := x * sin(x)$\na_int : 0$ b_int : float(%pi)$\nn_subdiv : 12$\nh : (b_int - a_int) / n_subdiv$\n\n/* On each subinterval, sup and inf require some care.  For x sin(x) on [0,π]\n   the function is positive and unimodal-ish; we'll sample many points within\n   each subinterval to find sup/inf empirically (good enough for visualisation). */\nsample_per_sub : 50$\n\nupper_sum : 0.0$ lower_sum : 0.0$ mid_sum : 0.0$\nupper_xs : []$  upper_ys : []$\nlower_xs : []$  lower_ys : []$\nfor i : 1 thru n_subdiv do block([xL, xR, sub_pts, sub_vals, sup_v, inf_v, x_mid],\n  xL : a_int + (i - 1) * h,\n  xR : xL + h,\n  sub_pts : np_to_list(np_linspace(xL, xR, sample_per_sub)),\n  sub_vals : map(lambda([x], float(f_riem(x))), sub_pts),\n  sup_v : lmax(sub_vals),\n  inf_v : lmin(sub_vals),\n  x_mid : 0.5 * (xL + xR),\n  upper_sum : upper_sum + sup_v * h,\n  lower_sum : lower_sum + inf_v * h,\n  mid_sum : mid_sum + float(f_riem(x_mid)) * h,\n  upper_xs : append(upper_xs, [xL, xR]),\n  upper_ys : append(upper_ys, [sup_v, sup_v]),\n  lower_xs : append(lower_xs, [xL, xR]),\n  lower_ys : append(lower_ys, [inf_v, inf_v]))$\n\nprint(\"U(f, P) =\", upper_sum)$\nprint(\"L(f, P) =\", lower_sum)$\nprint(\"mid sum =\", mid_sum)$\ntrue_val : float(integrate(f_riem(x), x, a_int, b_int))$\nprint(\"∫₀^π x sin(x) dx (true) =\", true_val)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 20,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "U(f, P) = 3.6000257034637064\nL(f, P) = 2.6487771127090256\nmid sum = 3.1505823445670273\nrat: replaced 3.141592653589793 by 80143857/25510582 = 3.1415926535897927\nrat: replaced 3.141592653589793 by 80143857/25510582 = 3.1415926535897927\nrat: replaced 3.141592653589793 by 80143857/25510582 = 3.1415926535897927\nrat: replaced 3.141592653589793 by 80143857/25510582 = 3.1415926535897927\nrat: replaced 3.141592653589793 by 80143857/25510582 = 3.1415926535897927\nrat: replaced 3.141592653589793 by 80143857/25510582 = 3.1415926535897927\nrat: replaced 3.141592653589793 by 80143857/25510582 = 3.1415926535897927\nrat: replaced 3.141592653589793 by 80143857/25510582 = 3.1415926535897927\n∫₀^π x sin(x) dx (true) = 3.1415926535897927"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Visualise the squeeze\n\nLower sum is below the curve, upper sum above. The integral is sandwiched between them; as $n$ increases, the gap closes.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "x_curve : np_to_list(np_linspace(a_int, b_int, 300))$\ny_curve : map(lambda([x], float(f_riem(x))), x_curve)$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"lightblue\", line_width=2, name=\"upper sum (sup·h)\",\n  lines(upper_xs, upper_ys),\n  color=\"lightcoral\", line_width=2, name=\"lower sum (inf·h)\",\n  lines(lower_xs, lower_ys),\n  color=\"black\", line_width=2, name=\"f(x) = x sin(x)\",\n  lines(x_curve, y_curve),\n  title=\"Upper/lower Riemann sums sandwich the integral\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"f(x)\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 21,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
